WEBVTT

00:00:00.234 --> 00:00:02.926
This is PasteGuard for the MLH Solana Hackathon.

00:00:02.926 --> 00:00:06.695
A Pastebin comment promised twenty-five percent more on a crypto swap.

00:00:06.695 --> 00:00:10.033
To get the bonus, it told you to paste code into Tampermonkey.

00:00:10.753 --> 00:00:13.534
Tampermonkey lets scripts change the web pages you visit.

00:00:13.534 --> 00:00:15.778
Here, the script replaced the deposit address.

00:00:15.778 --> 00:00:19.437
The exchange still looked familiar, but a payment would go to the attacker.

00:00:20.123 --> 00:00:22.388
PasteGuard reads the code without running it.

00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:26.114
Click a finding to see the exact line that overwrites the deposit address.

00:00:26.804 --> 00:00:28.584
Now compare the two destinations.

00:00:28.584 --> 00:00:31.927
Solana devnet simulates the same payment once for each wallet.

00:00:31.927 --> 00:00:33.383
These are balance previews.

00:00:33.383 --> 00:00:35.163
No transaction is signed or sent.

00:00:35.848 --> 00:00:37.473
We built PasteGuard in one day.

00:00:37.473 --> 00:00:42.350
Try the safe reconstruction, paste your own script, or open one of the four documented cases.
